{
 "causes": {
  "estimator_conv_one_position": "estimate_onchip_fraction(metric='macs') counts every on-chip conv perceptron at one position: the conv mappers drive the shared perceptron through F.conv2d (conv2d_mapper.py:124-150), so the forward hook of _macs_breakdown (onchip_fraction.py:244-292) never fires and module_macs gets in_shape None (_num_positions returns 1, onchip_majority.py:78-86); the oracle counts conv MACs from FX shapes. MAC SSOT, owned by G1 (module_macs.py); not a census rule",
  "ir_emission_order": "the in-order partition follows IR emission order (partition_ir_graph, segmentation.py:29), which differs from FX order on the explicit-attention blocks; the dependency segmentation (compute_segment_ids, segmentation.py:132) gives the oracle's 30 at C0-C2",
  "no_convtranspose_mac_rule": "module_macs has no ConvTranspose rule (onchip_majority.py:117-142 returns 0), so the host ConvTranspose2d counts 0 MACs and the on-chip share reads 1.0 until S is declared",
  "no_matmul_mac_rule": "module_macs has no rule for a product of two activations (onchip_majority.py:117-142 returns 0), so the host matmuls count 0 MACs and the on-chip share reads 1.0; G1's Contraction declares forward_macs() (plan \u00a75.1), re-pinned at CL4"
 },
